      "observed": "C33 has value '10u' but its footprint is 'Coert-Vonk:CAP X7R 10nF ±10 100V 0603 Murata', description '10000 pF ±10% 100V Ceramic Capacitor X7R 0603 (1608 Metric)', and part number 'GRM188R72A103KA01J' (a 10nF capacitor).",
      "expected": "C33 should be a 10µF capacitor to match its value field and the other 10µF decoupling capacitors on the +3V3 rail (e.g., C30, C31, C36, C38).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C33\") (value \"10u\") (footprint \"Coert-Vonk:CAP X7R 10nF ±10 100V 0603 Murata\") (datasheet \"https://search.murata.co.jp/Ceramy/image/img/A01X/G101/ENG/GRM188R72A103KA01-02.pdf\") (description \"10000 pF ±10% 100V Ceramic Capacitor X7R 0603 (1608 Metric)\") ... (field (name \"PN\") \"GRM188R72A103KA01J\") ... (field (name \"Description\") \"10000 pF ±10% 100V Ceramic Capacitor X7R 0603 (1608 Metric)\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C33 +3V3 0 10u"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The +3V3 rail will have a 10nF decoupling capacitor instead of 10µF, potentially causing increased noise or instability on the 3.3V supply, affecting the ESP32, I2C bus, and TMC2209 logic.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain one clear anomaly: C33 is specified as a 10µF capacitor in its value field and in the SPICE deck, but its footprint, description, and part number are for a 10nF capacitor, so the assembled board would have a 10nF decoupling capacitor on the +3V3 rail instead of the intended 10µF."
}

